store_flashcards
store_concepts
store_notes
store_saved_mocks
store_ai_consultations
store_active_session
store_config

Do not change this conceptual architecture unless there is a genuine technical requirement.

3. BACKUP/RESTORE MUST SURVIVE THE ENTIRE REDESIGN.

Existing:
- Export Full Backup
- Restore Backup
- backup preview
- restore hydration
- data sanitization
- database restoration

must remain available.

Do not remove or hide these functions.

4. EVERY NEW FEATURE MUST WORK WITH THE EXISTING DATABASE.

Do not create a second question database.

Do not create a second knowledge-sheet database.

Do not create a second mock database.

Do not create a second Console database.

5. HUMAN UI AND AI CONSOLE MUST USE THE SAME UNDERLYING ENGINE.

If a feature exists in the UI, the Console should eventually be able to invoke the same capability.

If the Console can create a mock, it should use the same mock-generation engine as the UI.

If the UI can search questions, the Console should be able to search questions.

If the UI can create a question, the Console should be able to create a question.

Do not implement separate logic paths that behave differently.

6. FLASHCARDS ARE NOT A TRAINING ENGINE.

The Vault/flashcard functionality exists primarily as an Anki-export utility.

Do NOT build:
- spaced repetition
- in-app flashcard training analytics
- flashcard scheduling
- flashcard review engine
- flashcard weakness engine

The existing flashcard/Vault functionality should remain usable and searchable, but it is not the focus of the new practice engine.

7. DO NOT BREAK EXISTING FEATURES JUST TO MAKE NEW FEATURES WORK.

Existing functionality should continue to work:
- Dashboard
- Dojo
- Knowledge Studio / Compendium
- Synapse
- Console
- Vault
- question editing
- knowledge-sheet editing
- backup
- restore
- saved mocks
- mock review
- attempts
- exports

8. DO NOT ASSUME THAT THE CURRENT TAXONOMY IS PERFECT.

The application must support user-controlled taxonomy.

The user must be able to:
- add chapters
- edit chapter names
- delete chapters
- add subjects
- edit subjects
- delete subjects where safe
- reorganize content

The system must not force obsolete hardcoded chapters to remain forever.

However:

Deleting a taxonomy entry must NOT automatically delete the questions or knowledge sheets associated with it.

Taxonomy deletion and data deletion are separate operations.

