5. DATABASE MIGRATION RULE
================================================================================

If a schema change is genuinely necessary:

INCREMENT DB_VERSION.

Use IndexedDB's normal onupgradeneeded mechanism.

Never:
- delete all records
- recreate all stores
- rebuild everything from JSON unless explicitly restoring

Migration should be additive whenever possible.

For example:

OLD:
store_saved_mocks

NEW:
same store
+
new optional properties

rather than:

DELETE store_saved_mocks
CREATE store_saved_mocks again

Existing records should continue to deserialize safely.

All new fields should have sensible defaults.

Example:

old record:
{
  id,
  title,
  questions
}

new record:
{
  id,
  title,
  questions,
  selectionRule: null,
  randomize: false,
  generatedBy: "manual"
}

Old records must continue working.

